.TH BUFFER_CHUNKED 3
.SH NAME
buffer_chunked \- filter a buffered input for HTTP chunked encoding
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <http.h>
.PP
.BI "int buffer_chunked(buffer* " b ", buffer* " other ");"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B buffer_chunked
initializes the buffer
.I b
to act as a filter for the input source
.IR other ,
which is expected to provide data in HTTP chunked transfer encoding.
.PP
The filter transparently decodes the chunked stream, stripping chunk size headers and extensions, so that subsequent read operations on
.I b
retrieve only the raw data content.
.PP
The underlying
.I other
buffer should already be initialized. When
.I b
is closed, it will automatically handle deinitialization of its internal state, though the
.I other
buffer remains open.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns 1 on success, or 0 if memory allocation for the internal context fails.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR buffer (3),
.BR buffer_init (3),
.BR buffer_getline (3)